# Documentation maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** behavior (features, routes, validation, DB schema/migrations, env vars, integrations, or user-visible flows), **update documentation in the same change**.

**Claude Code:** invoke **`documentation-maintenance`** skill before claiming done.

## What to update

| Change type | Update |
| ----------- | ------ |
| Architecture, routes, env, API, data model | **`docs/PROJECT.md`** |
| Page/section UX in `src/` | **`docs/guides/routes/*.md`** (`route-guides` skill) |
| Ops / backup / cutover | **`docs/archive/operations/`** |
| Agent path pointers | **`.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc`** |

## Rules of thumb

- Small accurate edits over full rewrites.
- New env var or HTTP route → document in `docs/PROJECT.md`.
- Fix contradictions; do not leave docs stale.

## Exempt

Typos, internal renames with no behavior/API/UX impact.
